description:
In repos/activity-api/src/routes/activities.ts, make the POST /executions handler co-write a trace_digest row, mirroring the fire-and-forget pattern already used one line below for incrementTraceStoreCounter.

Insert the new statement immediately BEFORE this existing line, which occurs exactly once in the file:
    // trace_store_counters bookkeeping (migration 156) — fire-and-forget,

Insert exactly this code, followed by one blank line:

    // DIGEST CO-WRITE: trace_digest had exactly one writer, the POST / handler of the
    // execution-traces router, so executions recorded through THIS route were never
    // digested. Measured 2026-09-12: activity feature_compose had 2491 execution rows
    // and ZERO trace_digest rows, and execution_exemplar is extracted only from digests,
    // so the highest-traffic authoring activity was invisible to the extraction stage.
    // Dynamic import avoids a static cycle between the two route modules.
    // FAIL-OPEN and fire-and-forget: never blocks or fails the execution write.
    void import("./execution-traces").then((m) => m.insertTraceDigest({ execution_id: executionId, activity_id: activityIdFromRequest, success: validated.success, duration_ms: validated.duration_ms ?? 0, cost_usd: 0, org_id: orgId ?? "public", executed_at: new Date().toISOString() }, body)).catch(() => {});

WHY THESE VALUES: trace_digest requires execution_id, activity_id, org_id and success, and its duration_ms, cost_usd and executed_at fields use VALUE-OR defaults which do NOT fire on INSERT INTO with an object literal, so every one is supplied explicitly. insertTraceDigest was exported for this purpose in the immediately preceding commit.

All identifiers used already exist in this handler: executionId, activityIdFromRequest, validated, orgId and body. Introduce no new const or let. Do not change any other line in the file.

POST-CONDITION: after this change the file contains the exact string DIGEST CO-WRITE, the statement sits immediately above the trace_store_counters comment, and the file typechecks clean.

